# ============================================================================
# Hierarchies of the benchmark model. Every link is many-to-one and every
# path is balanced. Members and their parents live in the benchmark dataset,
# not here. Fixed member lists that belong to the model are in dimensions/*.csv.
# ============================================================================

# Product. A Material is one ERP code, for example a promo pack or a new
# artwork. Several materials make one planning SKU, the level plans use.
link Material -> SKU : n:1

# Category path: SKU -> Product Line -> Subcategory -> Category -> Division
link SKU -> "Product Line" : n:1
link "Product Line" -> Subcategory : n:1
link Subcategory -> Category : n:1
link Category -> Division : n:1

# Brand path, from the product line, so one brand can span categories
link "Product Line" -> Brand : n:1
link Brand -> "Brand Group" : n:1
link Brand -> "Brand Type" : n:1

# SKU attributes. Temperature zone also weights the logistics allocation.
link SKU -> "Pack Format" : n:1
link SKU -> "Size Band" : n:1
link SKU -> "Price Tier" : n:1
link SKU -> "Temperature Zone" : n:1
link SKU -> "Lifecycle Status" : n:1
link SKU -> Plant : n:1
link Plant -> "Supply Type" : n:1
# No Plant -> Country link on purpose. It would give the sales grain a second
# path to Country, next to Customer -> Customer Group -> Country. The engine
# then rolls customer sales up by the plant's country without any warning.

# Customer is the sold-to account, the party that places the order. A chain's
# buying company is one account. Its warehouses and stores are delivery
# addresses and are not in the model. A shop, kiosk or restaurant that orders
# for itself is its own account.
# Customer Group is the node that holds the trade agreement, inside one
# country. It is a chain's head office, a buying group, a wholesaler or a
# cluster of independent shops. Rates, fees and deductions sit here.
# The group fixes the country and so the currency. Amounts booked only on the
# group, such as a fee for a brand nobody bought yet, still reach the right
# country this way.
# Region is the sales territory, inside one country.
#
# Trade and geography: Customer -> Customer Group -> Channel
#                      Customer -> Customer Group -> Country -> Currency
# Territory:           Customer -> Region
link Customer -> "Customer Group" : n:1
link "Customer Group" -> Channel : n:1
link "Customer Group" -> Country : n:1
link Country -> Currency : n:1
link Customer -> Region : n:1
# No Region -> Country link on purpose. It would give the sales grain a second
# path to Country, and the engine would then pick one of them without a warning.

# A cost center has three parents. Channel is NULL (Channel) unless the
# cost center is a sales team that serves one channel.
link "Cost Center" -> Function : n:1
link "Cost Center" -> Country : n:1
link "Cost Center" -> Channel : n:1

# General ledger accounts for operating expenses
link Account -> "Account Group" : n:1
